Near the sea, there is a narrow lane.
I walk on this lane.
Here is an old sweets shop.
I enter the shop.
There is a worker in the shop.
I say to him, "Namaste bhaiya."
"I need to get to the office."
"Sweets are needed for everyone at the office."
"Are there fresh Maharashtrian pedha sweets here?"
The worker smiles.
He says, "Yes madam, there are fresh pedha sweets here."
I say, "Please give one box of pedhas."
He gives me the box.
I ask him, "How many rupees?"
He says, "Two hundred rupees."
I give two hundred rupees.
I put the box in my bag.
Today my journey by bus and metro is complete.
I am very happy.
